  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ナンバンサイカチ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%8A%E3%83%B3%E3%83%90%E3%83%B3%E3%82%B5%E3%82%A4%E3%82%AB%E3%83%81",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 107260568,
      "text": "ナンバンサイカチ は、インド（アッサム州、ヒマラヤ地域を含む）、スリランカ、バングラデシュ、ミャンマーが原産のマメ科の落葉樹で、黄色い5弁の花を付ける。満開の時期には、まるで黄色いシャワーを浴びているようなところから、ゴールデン・シャワーまたはゴールデンシャワー・ツリーの別名を持つ。果実は薬用とされ、樹皮からはタンニンが採取される。日本では沖縄、 奄美群島 、小笠原諸島以外では開花しない。タイの国花。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Cassia fistula」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cassia_fistula",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1373243581,
      "text": "Cassia fistula, also known as golden shower, purging cassia, Indian laburnum, kani konna, or pudding-pipe tree, is a flowering plant in the family Fabaceae. The species is native to the Indian subcontinent and adjacent regions of Southeast Asia. It is the national tree and flower of Thailand and the state flower of Kerala state in India. It is also a popular ornamental plant and is also used in herbal medicine."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "cultivation": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Cassia fistula」の節「Cultivation」",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cassia_fistula#Cultivation",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
        "revision": 1373243581,
        "heading": "Cultivation",
        "text": "Cassia fistula is widely grown as an ornamental plant in tropical and subtropical areas. It blooms in late spring/early summer in hot, dry weather. Flowering is profuse, with trees being covered with yellow flowers, many times with almost no visible leaves. It grows well in dry climates. Growth for this tree is best in full sun on well-drained soil; it is relatively drought-tolerant and slightly salt-tolerant. It will tolerate light brief frost, but can get damaged if the cold persists. It can be subject to mildew or leaf spot, especially during the second half of the growing season. The tree blooms better with pronounced differences between summer and winter temperatures.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
  },
